{"id": "P00361", "name": "Michael Sabel", "name_chinese": "Mike Sabel", "country": "United States", "net_worth_usd_m": "13004.2", "net_worth_source": "Forbes real-time", "source_of_wealth": "oil & gas", "industry": "energy", "sec_insider_companies": "", "shared_with": "", "appears_on": "Forbes real-time (2026); Forbes real-time (former) (2025); Forbes annual (2025); Hurun Global (2026); Wikidata (2025)", "focus": ["energy"], "forbes_profile_url": "https://www.forbes.com/profile/michael-sabel/", "wikidata_url": "http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q136480351", "forbes_bio": ["Mike Sabel cofounded liquified natural gas exporter Venture Global with former lawyer Bob Pender in 2013.", "Together they own more than 80% of the company, which went public at a nearly $60 billion valuation in January 2025.", "Sabel and Pender serve as Venture Global's executive co-chairmen. They worked together as co-CEOs until 2020 when Pender retired from the role and Sabel became sole chief executive.", "Before cofounding Venture Global, Sabel worked as an investment banker."], "forbes_facts": []}
{"id": "P01657", "name": "Adarsh Hiremath", "name_chinese": "Adarsh Hiremath", "country": "United States", "net_worth_usd_m": "4200.0", "net_worth_source": "Forbes real-time", "source_of_wealth": "AI Software", "industry": "technology", "sec_insider_companies": "", "shared_with": "", "appears_on": "Forbes real-time (2026); Hurun Global (2026); Hurun Global U40 (2026); Hurun Unicorn founders (2025-2026)", "focus": ["data_center_ai"], "forbes_profile_url": "https://www.forbes.com/profile/adarsh-hiremath/", "wikidata_url": "", "forbes_bio": ["Adarsh Hiremath is a cofounder of Mercor, a recruiting startup that helps Silicon Valley's biggest AI labs train their models.", "Hiremath and his cofounders Brendan Foody and Surya Midha became the world's three youngest self-made billionaires in October 2025, when private investors valued Mercor at $10 billion. All three were 22 at the time, but Midha is the youngest by roughly two months.", "Foody serves as CEO of Mercor, while Hiremath serves as chief technology officer. Midha transitioned from his role as chief operating officer to become the company's chairman in October 2025.", "Foody, Hiremath and Midha founded Mercor in 2023. Each cofounder owns an estimated 22% stake in the company.", "In September 2025, Mercor announced the company had hit $500 million in annualized revenue, up from $100 million in March."], "forbes_facts": []}
